{
  "id": "utopia-2419",
  "title": "UTOPIA 2419",
  "subtitle": "A Dystopian AI Art Adventure",
  "backgroundColor": "#030303",
  "summary": "An interactive dystopian tragedy told through 538 AI-assisted illustrations, a branching 160,000-word narrative and an original eleven-track score.",
  "statement": "A personal story about idealism, freedom and the moment a dream becomes a system of control.",
  "body": "Completed in June 2022, UTOPIA 2419 adapts my dystopian science-fiction novella Ideal Republic 2419 into an interactive web experience. Set in the twenty-fourth-century wasteland of Kapia, the story follows a protagonist who exposes false deities and leads a revolution in pursuit of an ideal republic. Their resistance gradually hardens into obsession, betrayal and tyranny, ending in cosmic exile and self-destruction.\n\nThe project examines the paradox of idealism: the desire for perfection can erase human complexity, turn belief into dogma and transform liberation into another form of oppression. I shaped the world through AI-assisted image generation, 3D modelling, rendering, texturing and detailed post-production, then connected its 538 illustrations through a choice-driven website with 683 interaction points, 12 narrative decisions and five interaction modes. The project was interviewed and featured by Beijing-based technology media company PingWest.",
